    <DataNode elementId="AT1G74540-MONOMER" textLabel="CYP98A8" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9CA61" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, zhang">Metabolite profiles were compared between a T-DNA insertion knock-out line of CYP98A8 and the wild type plants |CITS: [19762055]|. In the mutant, the production of trihydroxyferuloyl spermidine and dihydroxyferuloylsinapoyl spermidine was replaced by triferuloyl spermidine, which suggested CYP98A8 functions in the hydroxylation of triferuloyl spermidine. Similarly, increased accumulation of tricoumaroyl spermidine was found in the mutant, indicating that CYP98A8 is also involved in the hydroxylation step of tricoumaroyl spermidine.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G74540-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G74540.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9CA61" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33214, RXN-33213, RXN-33212, RXN-17500, RXN-17499" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="5" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G74540.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G74540" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_19762055" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT5G54160-MONOMER" textLabel="Flavone 3&apos;-O-methyltransferase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT5G54160.1" dataSource="TAIR gene name" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">This enzyme has been shown to act as a 3&apos;-O-methyltransferase on a variety of substrates, based both on in vitro assays and mutant phenotypes. The substrates characterized to date are quercetin |CITS: [10700397][12777055]|, myricetin |CITS:[10700397]|, and caffeic acid, 5-OH-ferulic acid, 5-OH-coniferaldehyde, and 5-OH-coniferyl alcohol |CITS:[12777055]|. Another papers identifies the enzyme as a flavonol 3&apos;-methyltransferase |CITS: [10700397]|.</Comment>
